Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nf_flow_table: do not resurrect a dying network namespace
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

The platform FDB roaming notifier can be called from cleanup_net after
the namespace active reference count has reached zero. get_net() then
triggers addition-on-zero, and the deferred worker later underflows the
saturated count with put_net().

Use maybe_get_net() to atomically acquire only a live namespace. If it
fails, release the unqueued cleanup object. A successful acquisition is
still balanced by the existing cleanup worker put_net().

Applies after 990-01-smartrg-netfilter-nf_flow_table-invalidate-flows-on-
bridge-FDB-roaming.patch. No PPE policy, bridge VLAN or mt76 changes.

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
@@ -850,7 +850,12 @@
 	if (!cleanup)
 		return;
 
-	cleanup->net = get_net(net);
+	/* FDB deletion also runs while a network namespace is exiting. */
+	cleanup->net = maybe_get_net(net);
+	if (!cleanup->net) {
+		kfree(cleanup);
+		return;
+	}
 	memcpy(cleanup->mac, mac, ETH_ALEN);
 	INIT_WORK(&cleanup->work, nf_flow_table_mac_cleanup_work);
 	queue_work(flow_mac_cleanup_wq, &cleanup->work);
